   "html_text": "It is common to formulate Mary’s new knowledge in terms of Thomas Nagel’s famous locution of knowing what it’s like: Mary does not know (while living in her black-and-white environment) what it is like to see colors and she learns what it is like to see colors only after her release. But this common way to put the point may lead to a confusion of (a) mere acquaintance with kinds of color experiences by having and remembering them and (b) knowledge about what kind of color experience other subjec",
